{# ===========================================================================
   Component: location-menu

   Section 4 of the location page template in SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md: this
   room's menu.

   IT IS THE ROOM'S FULL MENU NOW, 2026-09-16, AND IT COMES FROM TOAST.

   It used to be menu.json filtered by a `locations` array, which made every
   room's page a view onto one reconciled catalog that never reconciled. The
   division of labour changed: /menu/ carries the signature and core dishes
   and says where one is missing, a location page carries THAT ROOM'S FULL
   MENU, and Toast stays the live authority. Rows come from
   src/_data/roomMenus.js, which reads the room's own Toast catalog, drops the
   non-dish rows, joins each row through src/_data/menuAliases.json for its
   dietary marks and its photograph, and resolves the description from this
   room's Toast, then Convoy's, then menu.json.

   A SNAPSHOT, AND THE PAGE SAYS SO. The catalogs were pulled 2026-08-04.
   Nothing here fetches, the heading does not promise completeness, and the
   room links to its own Toast page for the current list.

   USAGE
     {% set menuLoc = loc.id %}
     {% include "components/location-menu.njk" %}

   NO PRICES. Not here and not anywhere. They are in the catalogs, they are
   not read, and menuConcepts.json `_prices` has the history.
   =========================================================================== #}
{%- set room = roomMenus.byRoom[menuLoc] %}
{%- set roomLoc = (locations.items | where("id", menuLoc)) | first %}
{%- if room and room.sections | length %}
{#- id="menu" IS LOAD-BEARING. /menu/ is a room chooser, so a "see the menu"
    link on a room page that points there asks a reader standing in Convoy to
    pick a room. Six links across the NAP plate, both full location templates,
    the stub and the Maui order close point at #menu, which is this section on
    the page they are already on. -#}
<section class="sect" id="menu" aria-labelledby="menu-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <h2 class="u-visually-hidden" id="menu-title">The menu at {{ roomLoc.name }}</h2>
    <div class="mc mc--inline">
      {%- set mcLoc = menuLoc %}
      {%- set mcChrome = false %}
      {%- set mcSections = room.sections %}
      {%- set variant = mcVariantOverride | default(menuVariants.byRoom[menuLoc].variant) %}
      {%- set showPrices = false %}
      {% include "components/menu-concept.njk" %}
    </div>

    {#- ORDERING AND THE LIVE LIST, together, because they are the same answer.
        The rows above are a snapshot; this is where the menu actually is. -#}
    <div class="mc-live">
      <p class="mc-live__text">
        {%- if roomLoc.drinks and roomLoc.drinks.note %}
        {{ roomLoc.drinks.note }}
        {%- elif room.drinks.alcoholic %}
        {{ room.drinks.kinds | drinkLine }}{% if room.drinks.onTap %} on tap{% endif %}.
        {%- endif %}
        For the current menu and to order, {{ roomLoc.name }} is on Toast.
      </p>
      <a class="mc-live__cta" href="{{ roomLoc.orderUrl }}" rel="noopener">
        Order from {{ roomLoc.name }}
        <span aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
